Section 1. DEFINITIONS
================================================================

1.1. ILL Files - all program modules, source and object code,
documentation, configuration files, build scripts, graphical,
audio and other resources that are placed under this License
by their copyright holder and are identified as ILL Files in
the per-component list of the distribution or in per-file or
per-directory notices. Each ILL File indicates its Author.

1.2. Author - the copyright holder who has placed ILL Files
under this License. "Original Author" - the Author who first
published the Product under ILL.

1.3. Product - the ILL Files of an Author as published by
that Author, including the ILL Files as incorporated in any
Derivative Work. Third-Party Components are not part of the
Product.

1.4. Third-Party Components - components included in a
Distribution under licenses other than ILL, identified as such
in the per-component list in the NOTICE file.

1.5. Distribution - making the Product and Third-Party
Components available to the public or to third parties as one
aggregate (one installation image, repository, package
archive or storage medium), in any form and through any
means, including over networks (download, streaming, hosted
access). "Distribution" includes "making available to the
public" and "communication to the public" within the meaning
of applicable copyright law.

1.6. Modification - any change, adaptation, translation,
addition, deletion or other transformation of ILL Files or
their parts resulting in a work based on them. "Modifying
Author" - an Author who creates a Modification. The
authorship of a Modification is claimed by the person or
entity that directs and takes responsibility for the changes;
the use of software tools, including AI-assisted tools, does
not by itself create or negate authorship, which is determined
in accordance with applicable copyright law.

1.7. Derivative Work - a work that actually incorporates
copyright-protected elements of ILL Files (source or object
code, protected structure, sequence and organization of
code, and other original non-textual elements) and that
would, absent permission, infringe copyright.

    A work that interacts with the ILL Files solely through
documented public program interfaces (APIs), without copying
protected code or structure, is not a Derivative Work only
if ALL of the following conditions are met: (a) the
interaction is not the work's primary functional purpose;
(b) the work does not replace, reproduce or expose the
functionality of the ILL Files to third parties, including
as a hosted service, wrapper, shell, proxy, bridge,
plugin or user interface whose principal value is access
to the functionality of the Product; and (c) the work's
value to its users does not derive predominantly from
access to the functionality of the ILL Files. A work that
merely wraps, hosts, re-brands, configures or thinly
extends the ILL Files, or that makes the functionality of
the ILL Files available to third parties by any technical
means, is a Derivative Work regardless of the absence of
copied code. Mere renaming, re-packaging, parameterization
or change of delivery channel (including network delivery)
of the ILL Files does not create an independent work. A
fully independent implementation of the same functionality,
created without access to the source code of the ILL Files,
is likewise not a Derivative Work.

    Interaction of a Third-Party Component (including a
component under a strong-copyleft license such as the GNU
General Public License) with ILL Files solely through
documented public program interfaces, ordinary process
boundaries or standard system calls does not make the
Third-Party Component a Derivative Work of the ILL Files,
does not subject the Third-Party Component to this License
in any respect, and does not restrict the exercise of the
rights granted under the Third-Party Component's own
license. Nothing in this License may be read as extending
the Non-Commercial Use restriction, the fee prohibition or
any other condition of this License to a Third-Party
Component (see Sections 2.2 and 2.4).

1.8. Authorship Chain - the ordered, cumulative record of
authorship of the Product and of every Modification of it,
starting with the Original Author and continuing with every
Modifying Author in order of modification. For each author
the chain indicates: (a) the name or a stable pseudonym;
(b) the date or release version of the contribution;
(c) a brief indication of the changes made; and (d) at the
author's option, contact details. The chain is kept in the
NOTICE (or AUTHORS) file and/or in per-file headers
customary for the medium. A Modifying Author is included in
the chain upon a consent mark (CONTRIBUTING, section 3); a
contribution merged without a consent mark is included only
once the contributor has confirmed the chain entry, and
until then the entry is marked "unconfirmed". An
unconfirmed entry does not confer standing under clause
4.7 until confirmed; the validity of the License Stack
is not otherwise affected. A contribution merged
without a consent mark is not an ILL File and is not
licensed under this License or the License Stack until
its chain entry is confirmed; until then it is excluded
from the Product for the purposes of the grants in
Sections 3 and 10 and must not be distributed as part of
the Product. The Authors shall, upon discovery,
promptly remove or replace unconfirmed contributions.

    A recipient who obtained the Product or a Derivative Work
in compliance with the License Stack as stated in the root
LICENSE, NOTICE and MODULES files (clause 6.8) is not in
breach by reason of a contribution later determined to be
unconfirmed, provided that upon discovery or written notice
the recipient promptly removes or replaces the unconfirmed
contribution in all further distributions within the
recipient's reasonable control. The exclusion of an
unconfirmed contribution does not affect the rights under
this License of recipients who obtained the Product or a
Derivative Work before the chain entry was marked
unconfirmed, provided they comply with the License Stack.

1.9. Supplemental Terms ("Module") - additional license terms
attached by an Author to the Product or to specifically
identified parts of it in accordance with Section 6.

1.10. License Stack - for any ILL File or Modification: this
base License plus all Modules of the Authors in the
Authorship Chain applicable to that file, attached in the
order of the chain.

1.11. Commercial Use - any use of the Product or a Derivative
Work other than Non-Commercial Use, including but not limited
to: use by legal entities, sole traders and government
bodies; providing access over networks (SaaS, hosting, VDI)
for remuneration or in the course of commercial activity;
distribution, resale, embedding in equipment; use as a tool
for providing commercial services; use by natural persons
for providing services for remuneration regardless of
entrepreneur status; and fundraising with the help of the
Product (crowdfunding, donations solicited in connection
with the Product); and use of the Product, including its
source code, to train, fine-tune or evaluate
machine-learning models in the course of commercial
activity. Receiving advertising revenue in
connection with demonstrations of the Product is Commercial
Use.

    A use is presumed Commercial where the Product is used:
on the equipment of an organization, in its internal network
or under its account, if the use forms part of the tasks or
commercial interests of that organization; by a natural
person for the purpose of obtaining profit or remuneration;
by a natural person on equipment or infrastructure provided
by an organization, if the use forms part of that person's
assigned duties or of the tasks or commercial interests of
that organization; or in the provision of services to third
parties, including free-of-charge provision if it promotes
other commercial interests (customer acquisition, advertising
of commercial offers).

    The following are not presumed Commercial ("Safe
Harbors"; the User bears the burden of showing that a Safe
Harbor applies): (a) personal, non-remunerated use by a
natural person, including incidental use on equipment
provided by an organization where such personal use is
permitted by that organization's rules and does not form
part of the person's assigned duties; (b) verbatim
reproduction and redistribution of the Product without
monetization, without advertising and without promotion of
commercial interests, including mirrors, forks and package
archives; (c) demonstration and review of the Product where
any advertising revenue derives from the reviewer's platform
as a whole and not specifically from the demonstration of
the Product itself.

1.12. Non-Commercial Use - use of the Product or a Derivative
Work exclusively for personal, educational, research,
civic/charitable and other purposes not aimed at obtaining
profit or remuneration and not falling within the definition
of Commercial Use. Without limiting the Safe Harbors of
clause 1.11, hosting of the Product or of a Derivative Work
with free access, without advertising and without promotion
of commercial interests constitutes Non-Commercial Use
(see Annex 1, example (14)).

1.13. User - a natural or legal person exercising the rights
granted by this License.

1.14. Complete Corresponding Source Code - the complete
source code of the ILL Files distributed in object code
form, in the preferred form for making modifications,
including all modules, interface definition files and
scripts used to control compilation and installation of the
object code, and the scripts controlling the Product's
start, provided that such scripts are distributed as part
of the Product. Source code of Third-Party Components is
governed by their own licenses.

1.15. Affiliate - an entity that controls, is controlled by,
or is under common control with a person, where control
means ownership of more than fifty per cent of voting rights
or equity, or the power to direct the management and
policies of an entity.

1.16. Commercial Rightsholder - the Author, or the person or
entity designated under clause 8.2, that is entitled to
conclude Commercial Agreements for given ILL Files.

