Section 2. SCOPE: PER-COMPONENT APPLICATION
================================================================

2.1. This License applies exclusively to ILL Files and never
applies to Third-Party Components. In particular:
(a) each Third-Party Component remains licensed solely under
    its own license, and the terms of that license are
    unaffected by this License;
(b) no provision of this License restricts, conditions,
    narrows or revokes any right granted under the license of
    a Third-Party Component; in particular, no field-of-use
    restriction (including the prohibition of Commercial
    Use) and no fee obligation under this License applies to
    Third-Party Components, and nothing in this License is
    construed as relicensing a Third-Party Component;
(c) no party may state or imply that a Third-Party Component
    is licensed under ILL, or that ILL Files are licensed
    under the license of a Third-Party Component.

2.2. Mere aggregation is permitted. Making a Distribution
available (one installation image, repository, package
archive or storage medium containing ILL Files together
with Third-Party Components, including components under
strong-copyleft licenses) is permitted, provided that each
component remains an independent work identifiable per file
or per package, and the license of each Third-Party
Component is complied with (including source-code and
notice obligations).

2.3. Combining ILL Files with a strong-copyleft Third-Party
Component through linking, inclusion in one program, or
derivation is permitted only in a manner that does not,
under the terms of that copyleft license, subject the ILL
Files to the copyleft license. Where such a combination
does, by operation of the copyleft license, extend to the
combined work, the ILL Files included in that combination
are, with respect to that combined work, licensed under
the copyleft license by each affected Author to the
extent necessary to comply with that copyleft license,
and the terms of the copyleft license prevail to the
extent of the conflict.

2.4. Independent communication between the Product and a
Third-Party Component through ordinary process boundaries,
documented public APIs or standard system calls does not
create a Derivative Work of that Third-Party Component and
does not subject the Product to its license.

