Chain file, in accordance with Section 8.

3.3. Direct rights. Rights under this License are granted to
the User directly by each Author. This License does not
limit rights the User holds under other licenses granted by
the same Author.

================================================================
Section 4. AUTHORSHIP CHAIN
================================================================

4.1. Traceability - the core condition. The defining
condition of this License is that the chain of authorship
remains clearly traceable from the Original Author through
every Modification. Every distributed copy of the Product or
of a Derivative Work must preserve the complete Authorship
Chain.

4.2. Form and maintenance of the chain.
(a) All copyright notices, this License, all applicable
    Modules and the warranty disclaimer are retained in all
    copies.
(b) The central Authorship Chain file (NOTICE or AUTHORS,
    at the root or per package) lists every Author in
    order, with the date or release version of the
    contribution and a brief description of the changes.
(c) Every Modification, before it is distributed, adds the
    Modifying Author's entry to the chain: name or stable
    pseudonym, date or version, brief description of the
    changes. Where per-file headers are customary in the
    relevant community, the modified files' headers are
    updated instead of or in addition to the central file.
(d) All changes to the files are clearly indicated and
    dated.

4.3. No removal. No User may remove, alter, obscure or
truncate any entry of the Authorship Chain or any copyright
notice or license reference, whether in the original files
or in any Modification. The preceding sentence does not
apply to (i) the removal or replacement of an unconfirmed
contribution or of its chain entry as required by clause
1.8, and (ii) the removal of a chain entry pursuant to a
data-protection order under clause 4.8; in both cases the
order and completeness of the chain are preserved by a
note recording the removal, in accordance with clause 4.8.
A change of naming or branding does
not extinguish the chain: a new name is added on top of the
chain, never in place of it. Corrections of a chain entry
are made by an additional entry of the same Author
referencing the corrected entry, never by rewriting it.

4.4. Continued authorship. Each Author retains copyright in
that Author's own contributions and may use them
independently, provided they function without the ILL Files
of the other Authors. Copyright in the Product as a whole is
exercised in accordance with this License and the License
Stack.

4.5. Sanction. Removal or obscuring of Authorship Chain
entries or of copyright notices is a material breach of
this License and an infringement of the attribution rights
of every Author in the chain. It entails termination under
Section 13 and liability to each affected Author.

4.6. Moral rights. To the extent moral rights (including
droit moral and rights of attribution and integrity) cannot
be waived or assigned under applicable law, each Author
agrees not to assert them against Users who comply with the
License Stack. Where attribution is legally required,
attribution through the Authorship Chain is agreed to
satisfy that requirement to the fullest extent permitted.

4.7. Standing. Each Author may enforce this License with
respect to that Author's own contributions and the
integrity of the Authorship Chain as a whole. Authors are
not obliged to enforce, and no Author is liable for another
Author's decision not to enforce.

4.8. Privacy of chain entries. Chain entries contain
personal data only to the extent an Author chooses to
identify with a real name or contact details; pseudonymous
entries are the default. An Author may update or remove
that Author's contact details at any time without altering
the entry itself. Where mandatory data-protection law
grants rights of rectification or erasure, an entry is
corrected by a new entry (clause 4.3); where erasure is
finally ordered under mandatory law, the entry is removed
and its place in the order of the chain is recorded with
the note "entry removed pursuant to a data-protection
order", so that the order and completeness of the chain
remain verifiable. A pseudonymous entry is not invalidated
by the use of a pseudonym; the Author may prove authorship
for enforcement purposes by any credible evidence.

