Section 5. MODIFICATIONS: LICENSE INHERITANCE
================================================================

5.1. Every Modification and every Derivative Work that
incorporates ILL Files must, to the extent of that
incorporation, be governed by this License - the same
edition that governs the modified files (each file
indicates its edition; where it does not, the edition
referenced in the release documentation applies; where
neither exists, the edition referenced in the LICENSE or
NOTICE file distributed with the file applies; where none of
these exists, the edition current at the date of the
Modification applies) - together with the License Stack
accumulated in the Authorship Chain. A single file must not
combine content governed by different editions; where a file
without edition indication is modified, the Modification
states the edition applied.

5.2. No author, distributor or recipient may relicense,
sublicense or otherwise make ILL Files available under
different terms, and no additional condition may be imposed
that restricts exercise of the rights granted under this
License. The prohibition on additional conditions applies
to conditions imposed outside the License Stack:
Supplemental Terms attached in accordance with Section 6
are the exclusive means of adding conditions to ILL Files,
and are valid only within the limits of clauses 6.3 and
6.4. This clause does not apply to Third-Party
Components, which remain under their own licenses.

5.3. A Modification may be published and distributed
independently, subject to compliance with Sections 4-8.
Distribution under the License Stack is otherwise free of
charge for Non-Commercial Use, subject to clause 7.2.

================================================================
Section 6. MODULARITY: SUPPLEMENTAL TERMS
================================================================

6.1. Right to extend. ILL is a modular license. Any Author
may attach Supplemental Terms ("Module") to the Product or
to specifically identified own additions. A Module takes
effect when it is distributed together with the Authorship
Chain entry of its Author.

6.2. The License Stack. The effective license of any ILL
File or Modification is the License Stack: this base License
plus all Modules of the Authors in the chain applicable to
that file, in the order the chain was formed. All recipients
receive rights under the Stack.

6.3. Validity conditions. A Module is valid only if all of
the following are met:
(a) it expressly acknowledges that the ILL Files remain
    governed by this base License;
(b) it does not contradict this base License, including its
    Core Conditions (clause 6.4);
(c) it does not contradict, cancel, condition or restrict
    any Module of a previous Author in the chain: a later
    Module may only add terms, never remove rights granted
    by earlier Modules;
(d) it clearly identifies its Author (through the chain
    entry), the date of attachment and its scope - the
    specific files or additions to which it applies;
(e) it does not impose fees, royalties, account requirements
    or technical restrictions on Non-Commercial use,
    modification or distribution of the ILL Files
    themselves, and it does not grant or purport to grant
    Commercial Use rights: Commercial Use is available only
    under a Commercial Agreement under Section 8;
(f) it does not purport to relicense Third-Party
    Components;
(g) it does not require removal or obscuring of any
    copyright notice, license text or Authorship Chain
    entry;
(h) it does not impose field-of-use, ethical-use,
    visibility or attribution conditions on Non-Commercial
    use beyond what this base License itself requires
    (including any requirement of visible attribution in
    user interfaces, outputs or works created with the
    Product), and it does not require any technical or
    legal measure that would make compliance with an
    earlier Module or with the base License impossible.
A Module that fails any condition is void to the extent of
the conflict or impermissible restriction; the remainder of
the License Stack remains in force.

6.4. Core Conditions. No Module may contradict or weaken
the following conditions of this License:
(i)   preservation and completeness of the Authorship Chain
      (Section 4);
(ii)  the separation of Non-Commercial and Commercial Use
      (Sections 3 and 8);
(iii) license inheritance: every Modification carries this
      License and the License Stack (Section 5);
(iv)  per-component scope for Third-Party Components
      (Section 2);
(v)   the exclusion of warranties and the limitation of
      liability (Section 12).

6.5. Precedence. In case of conflict within a License Stack:
the base License prevails over any Module; earlier Modules
prevail over later Modules; and mandatory terms of
applicable law or of the license of a Third-Party Component
prevail over any term of the Stack to the extent of the
conflict. The conflicting part of the later term is void;
the remainder of the Stack applies.

6.6. MODULES file. All Modules are collected in a MODULES
file at the root of the repository (or per package, with a
manifest at the root), one Module per block, each referencing
its Author's chain entry. Every Distribution of the Product
or of a Derivative Work must pass on the current MODULES
file together with the copies. A Module not present in the
MODULES file of a Distribution does not bind recipients of
that Distribution, and a Module distributed without its
Author's chain entry is void. A Module, once distributed,
may not be withdrawn or amended; a correction is made by
a new Module of the same Author referencing the earlier one
(clause 4.3).

6.7. Exclusion of burdensome Modules. The Original Author
(or, failing that Author, the majority of the Authors
recorded in the Authorship Chain) may mark a Module
"excluded" in the central MODULES file, stating the reasons
in a new entry referencing the excluded Module (clause 4.3).
An excluded Module remains part of the historical record and
its chain entry is preserved, but it does not propagate to
Distributions made after the exclusion and does not bind
recipients of those Distributions. The exclusion affects
only the Module; the base License and all other Modules
remain in force. An exclusion under this clause does not
