Section 13. TERMINATION
================================================================

13.1. Upon a material breach by the User (Section 11.2),
the rights granted to the User under this License are
suspended automatically as of the breach. The rights
terminate: (a) immediately, in the cases listed in clause
13.2; (b) in any other case of material breach, at the end
of a 30-day cure period running from written notice from an
affected Author, if the breach is not cured within that
period, or upon written notice of termination from an
affected Author where the breach persists. Mere cessation
of the violating conduct does not by itself terminate the
suspension or restore the rights; reinstatement requires
the affirmative act described in clause 13.3.

13.2. Termination is immediate, without a cure period, in
case of circumvention of technical means of license
verification, imposition of restricting technical measures
under clause 11.1(e), or removal or alteration of
Authorship Chain entries or copyright notices that is
wilful or is not corrected within 30 days of written
notice from an affected Author. Removal or alteration of
Authorship Chain entries or copyright notices that is
inadvertent and non-prejudicial and is corrected within
that period is treated as a breach curable under clause
13.1(b); upon correction notified to the affected Author,
the rights of the User are reinstated automatically,
without the written confirmation otherwise required by
clause 13.3.

13.3. Reinstatement. If the User ceases all violation of
this License, the rights granted to that User are
reinstated only upon written confirmation from an affected
Author; no reinstatement occurs automatically, and the
rights remain terminated or suspended until reinstated in
writing. In the cases of clause 13.2 - except an inadvertent
breach reinstated automatically under the fourth sentence
of clause 13.2 - reinstatement is at the sole discretion
of the affected Author(s) and
additionally requires restoration of the affected notices,
chain entries and unrestricted copies insofar as they remain
within the User's reasonable control.

13.4. Termination of one User does not affect rights of
other recipients who obtained the Product or a Derivative
Work in compliance with this License, nor the licenses of
Third-Party Components under their own terms.

13.5. No failure or delay by an Author in enforcing this
License constitutes a waiver of any right under it.

13.6. Sections 4, 12 and 15 survive termination, as well as
any provisions that by their nature must survive.

13.7. Termination does not affect source-code offers already
made under clause 7.1(e), nor the rights of recipients under
clause 13.4.

